"Garden Hall is a Celena North High dorm on the edge of campus."
"It is gray stone with forest green shutters and tended ivy, like an enlarged English cottage."
"It rises three stories and has no elevators."
"Evergreens and a garden with grills, tables and student-labeled planters screen it from the street."
"The interface greets residents with 'Welcome Home' as they enter."
"The common area has concrete floors, tired sofas, shelves of books and games and a kitchen."
"A ground-floor mailroom with low postboxes sits beside the laundry."
"Suites have four bedrooms with loft beds; two bedrooms have windows, two have wall screens."
"Suites share a bath with a claw-footed tub, and have polished concrete floors and white walls."
"Suite furniture favors indestructibility over comfort, and inner walls aren't soundproofed."
"A heater disguised as a fireplace glows in colored logs in each suite's living area."
"Students may keep their suite through high school."
"An identical girls-only building faces it across a walkway."
"Alden shares a second-floor suite with Lexi, Haoyu and Lute Velra; Kon lives a floor above."
"The four furnished their living room as a winter hunting lodge, with a fake polar bear head."
